cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "thermoelectric-ledger: signed heat-flow accounting with withheld exergy and efficiency"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    email: partnerships@sparkainlp.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/thermoelectric-ledger"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  Research software that preserves signed electrical and hot-side heat-flow
  readings, exposes each uncertainty-adjusted heat-flow lower bound, and
  withholds Carnot/exergy and efficiency when those preconditions are
  unresolved. It is not a measurement campaign and not a thermoelectric
  device; it makes no claim that any device delivers more energy than it
  absorbs, and it is not a clinical or computing-hardware product.
  Synthetic demos are labelled and never receive an efficiency claim.
keywords:
  - research software
  - thermoelectric
  - heat-flow ledger
  - uncertainty bounds
  - exergy ceiling
  - signed measurements
  - New Brunswick
